<% title "Manage payments — #{@event.name}" %>

<%= render "events/nav", selected: :payments %>

<h1 class="heading">Manage payments</h1>

<%# Fuime: the embedded replacement for the Stripe Dashboard.

    Every account Fuime creates is `stripe_dashboard.type = none` — the guardian
    has no Stripe login and never sees stripe.com. That is deliberate (it keeps
    the family inside one product, and it means there is no second place where
    Fuime's rules do not apply), but it is only honest if everything a Dashboard
    would be needed for lives here. This page is that promise, kept.

    Guardian-only. Fuime::PaymentSetupsController gates it on `setup_payments?`,
    not on membership: these components show the account holder's own identity
    details and bank account, which is not information a teen on the venture is
    entitled to. %>

<p class="muted">
  This is everything you'd normally use a Stripe account for — your details, your
  bank account, your payouts and tax documents — without leaving Fuime.
  <%= link_to "Payment status", fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
</p>

<% unless @connected_account.livemode %>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    This is a Stripe <strong>test</strong> account — no real money can move through it.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%# One controller instance wraps the whole region so all four components share a
    single Account Session. See stripe_connect_component_controller.js for why
    that matters (one instance per component would mint one session per box). %>
<div
  data-controller="stripe-connect-component"
  data-stripe-connect-component-publishable-key-value="<%= @publishable_key %>"
  data-stripe-connect-component-session-url-value="<%= fuime_payment_setup_session_path(event_slug: @event.slug) %>">

  <%# Stripe's own "we need something from you" banner. First, because it is the
      only thing on this page that can tell a guardian their venture is about to
      stop working. The controller keeps it hidden until Stripe reports at least
      one notification, so an all-clear account shows no empty box. %>
  <div data-stripe-connect-component-target="mount" data-component="notification-banner" class="mb2" hidden></div>

  <h2 class="mt2">Your details</h2>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Your name, address and business details as Stripe holds them. Fuime never sees
    or stores any of it.
  </p>
  <div data-stripe-connect-component-target="mount" data-component="account-management" class="mb3"></div>

  <h2 class="mt2">Payouts and bank account</h2>
  <%# Read-only on purpose, and this note is the user-facing half of a rule
      enforced in MANAGEMENT_COMPONENTS: `standard_payouts` and
      `edit_payout_schedule` are off, so this component can show the balance,
      the history and the connected bank account, but cannot start a payout or
      switch the account to an automatic schedule. Both would route money around
      the approval flow that makes "the teen asks, the adult decides" real. %>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Money is paid out only when you approve a request, from
    <%= link_to "the payouts page", fuime_payouts_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
    You can change the bank account it goes to here.
  </p>
  <div data-stripe-connect-component-target="mount" data-component="payouts" class="mb3"></div>

  <h2 class="mt2">Tax documents</h2>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Any tax forms Stripe issues for this account, such as a 1099-K.
  </p>
  <div data-stripe-connect-component-target="mount" data-component="documents" class="mb3"></div>

  <%# Left in place if the components never mount — a page of empty headings gives
      a parent no way to tell "still loading" from "broken". %>
  <p data-stripe-connect-component-target="fallback" class="muted text-sm">
    Loading your payment tools…
    If nothing appears, check that your browser isn't blocking scripts from Stripe,
    then reload this page.
  </p>
</div>

<p class="muted text-sm mt-4">
  Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not hold
  deposits and does not offer FDIC-insured products. Payments are processed by
  Stripe into an account owned by
  <%= @event.institutionally_sponsored? ? "the sponsoring school" : "a parent or legal guardian" %>.
</p>
